verdicts.reason:
Verified against conf 10.2.0 and atomically 1.7.0. The `store` getter runs readFileSync + JSON.parse on every get(). set() re-reads, then atomically.writeFileSync does temp file, fsync and rename, with synchronous retries up to 100 ms. The per-drop count holds: 12 parses and 1 fsync'd write before the send at :352. The facade is safe:
- main.js only uses get and set (40 and 10 call sites), and no key contains a dot;
- links_update mutates the returned object, then set()s it;
- every other returned object is only read or structured-cloned by IPC;
- `diskStore.store = data` writes without the extra read.
The reorder (send first, then record) is safe. Skip the optional history debounce: on Windows, 'before-quit' is not emitted at shutdown or logoff.

Verified:
- :624-629 saves any key and type;
- both windows share the preload (:189, :243), and no handler checks the sender;
- :425-426 sends identity + token to the configured URL on open;
- {dropHistory:5} makes :117 throw.
The RULES match the UI exactly:
- settings.html ranges: volume and music 0-100 -> 0..1, opacity 20-100 -> 0.2..1, durations 1..30;
- the theme and avoid-zone options, HH:MM time inputs and numeric display ids;
- settings.js's key set, including {paused}.
overlay.js only uses getSettings, onDrop, onSettingsUpdate and onCursor, plus the overlay:*, stage-empty and drop:react channels. Settings only opens the github.com URL. Keeping the read-only handlers open is fine: none exposes the token.

