Add powerMonitor to the electron import at :2. In whenReady():
```js
// Au réveil, la socket d'avant la veille est presque toujours morte.
powerMonitor.on('resume', () => {
  if (store.get('paused')) return;
  reconnectAttempts = 0;
  if (reconnectTimer) clearTimeout(reconnectTimer);
  reconnectTimer = setTimeout(connectWS, 2000);   // laisse le Wi-Fi revenir
});
```
connectWS() clears reconnectTimer and drops the old socket without triggering its close handler. The register replaces the stale link on the bot (it kicks the old ws).

Bind the identity to the origin that issued it (local field only):
```js
const originOf = (u) => { try { const x = new URL(u); return `${x.protocol}//${x.host}`; } catch { return String(u); } };
// 'linked' (:455) : ajouter server: originOf(url) à l'objet stocké (links_update le conserve)
// 'open' (:425-426) :
const identity = store.get('linkIdentity'), here = originOf(url);
if (identity && identity.userId &&
    (!identity.server || identity.server === here || here === originOf(DEFAULT_SERVER))) {
  const { server, ...wire } = identity;   // le champ local ne part pas sur le fil
  wsSend({ type: 'register', identity: wire });
}
```
Legacy identities without `server` behave as today once, then get bound on the next 'linked'. The DEFAULT_SERVER exception keeps zero-touch re-link working across official server moves (e.g. the :58 migration).
